$HEADER_BEGIN
title: "owomd :3"
css_imports:
  - "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@400;700;900&display=swap"
  - "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@catppuccin/palette@1.0.0/css/catppuccin.css"
custom_css: |
  body {
    font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif;
    background-color: var(--ctp-macchiato-base, #24273a);
    color: var(--ctp-macchiato-text, #cad3f5);
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
  }
  a {
    color: var(--ctp-macchiato-pink, #f5bde6);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  h1, h2, h3 {
    color: var(--ctp-macchiato-mauve, #c6a0f6);
  }
  h1 {
    color: var(--ctp-macchiato-pink, #f5bde6);
    font-weight: 900;
  }
  img {
    max-width: 300px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
$HEADER_END

![owomd logo](owomd.png)

# owomd :3
*A custom markdown format and compiler for gays, by gays :3c.*

[View on GitHub](https://github.com/gayboi-club/owomd/) :3

## Features

$iterate features as f{
- **${f.title}**: ${f.desc}
}

## Getting Started

You can spin up the live development server or compile files statically using the binary :3

````bash
# 1. Start the live development server
./owomd serve . --port 8080

# 2. Or statically compile a file with dynamic data
cat data.json | ./owomd index.md.owo > index.html
````

## Beautiful Alerts

Built in support for GitHub style alerts :3c

> [!TIP]
> **Pro Tip :3**
> You can use these alerts to draw attention to important information in your documentation. They look absolutely stunning on dark mode :3

> [!WARNING]
> **Watch out :3c**
> Using `owomd` may cause an extreme urge to turn gay >~<

## Demo: Iterating Data :3

To show off the native JSON rendering capabilities, here is a webring list entirely generated from `data.json` using the `$iterate` syntax :3

$iterate webring as member{
- [${member.name}](${member.url})
}

